  WHY DEFERRED (full-app Xcode gate — ZERO ConnectionSegment errors; all blockers pre-exist this change):
    iOS  : the app target fails with exactly 2 errors, both "unable to resolve module dependency: 'XCTest'". Root
           cause is the established surface convention of CO-LOCATING *.Tests.swift next to the surface, which the
           XcodeGen path-based source inclusion compiles into the APP target (which does not link XCTest). This
           PRE-EXISTS this change: TeslaSync/feature-views already contributes 170 XCTest-importing *.Tests.swift
           files to the app target, so the app `build` was already XCTest-broken before shared-surfaces existed.
           (The companion collision documented in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md — `struct DashboardWidgetSize`
           redefined 15× across Sources/DashboardWidgets/* + TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets/* — is also present and
           unrelated; the XCTest module error short-circuits the build before type-checking reaches it.)
    macOS: fails with development-SIGNING errors ("TeslaSync-macOS"/"TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS" have entitlements that
           require signing with a development certificate), which this runner does not provision.
    These are exactly the artifacts apps/macos-pending-verifications.md defers to the ADR-012 macos-latest CI
    runner; they are owned by the P4/P99 Apple acceptance gate (signing + a *.Tests.swift→test-target routing pass
    + a dashboard-widget de-duplication pass), NOT by a single shared-surface prompt (task rule: do not fix
    pre-existing, unrelated breakage). grep of BOTH full-app build logs for "shared-surfaces|ConnectionSegment"
    intersected with "error:" = 0 hits. A pending-verification row is recorded in apps/macos-pending-verifications.md.

